  "id": "COMPOUND:25760 - PROTEIN:2333",
  "verbalization": "Sikokianin A is shown to have a target relationship with multiple entities, including Y79, mitogen-activated protein kinase kinase kinase 13, and ephrin type-A receptor 3. All of these entities are linked to the same compound, (1S,2S,5R,6R,7S,8S,11S)-7-hydroxy-5-(hydroxymethyl)-11-[(2R)-1-hydroxypropan-2-yl]-6-methyl-9-oxatricyclo[6.2.1.02,6]undecan-10-one, which in turn targets Mono-ADP-ribosyltransferase C3. This suggests a potential mechanism where Sikokianin A may act as a modulator of a signaling pathway involving this compound, possibly through the inhibition of its enzymatic activity. The shared target relationship across these entities implies a possible role for Sikokianin A in regulating a broader biological process, likely involving the modulation of signaling cascades that are central to cellular function. The evidence supports a direct interaction between Sikokianin A and Mono-ADP-ribosyltransferase C3, possibly through the inhibition of the enzyme's activity, which could have implications for therapeutic applications.",
